 "caveats": [
  "Singlet's value in the label metrics is its forced label (argmax_cl), the output every competitor gives. This column was chosen for the comparison after cxg16 was scored; the model and both columns were fixed before that. The published call (cell_type_cl) is reported separately as singlet-call.",
  "Two training choices of the network followed a first look at cxg16: calibrating the temperature on call reliability (on held-out Census collections) and trying tissue context (not used). See docs/celltype_nn.md section 4.",
  "Azimuth's own pretrained references cover 3 of the 16 studies' tissues; Seurat reference mapping with the shared Census reference stands for the Azimuth method on all 16.",
  "Thymic CD34+ progenitors (GSE144870) are the network's largest loss; on the authors' own matrix of these cells it scores 0.98 at depth 2, so the loss comes from reprocessing.",
  "Ding 2020 (7 protocols) and the 10x / mouse cohort sets listed for cell-type await the harness's Singlet counts."
 ],
